# Cyrius — Compiler Field Notes (Index)
# Compiler-internal training material for agents modifying or
# debugging the cyrius compiler. Topical organization (not
# chronological — for chrono narrative see retros/).
#
# Refreshed 2026-08-07 at v6.5.10 — DOC-CURRENCY SWEEP covering v6.5.7–.10, the
# releases these files had no entry for. This index had itself gone a full minor
# stale: its section counts read "11 methodology / 30 gotchas" against a live
# 16 / 116, and it still described the cx backend as having NO CLI surface, a
# premise retired at v6.4.17–.22. Counts below are now RE-DERIVED
# (`grep -c '^[[entries]]'`), not incremented — incrementing is how they drifted.
# WHAT .7–.10 ADDED: +9 gotchas, +2 methodology. The .7 through-line is that
# **five of the seven defects it found were HALF-FIXES that stopped at the first
# symptom** (AT_FDCWD corrected without its sibling flags; STAT_SIZE without the
# rest of the struct; unlink mapped without rmdir; three of four link syscalls
# routed) and every one surfaced the first time ONE new tcyr actually RAN on real
# ecb/ach hardware — `tests/tcyr/crossos/syscall_wrappers.tcyr`. New structural
# knowledge: the **>=1000 cyrius-private syscall alias band** on aarch64 (a number
# no OS mints, spelled 1000+native so it self-documents) and its ordering rule —
# ESYSXLAT is a linear cmp-chain that rewrites x8 in place, so an entry must sit
# BELOW every entry comparing the number it produces, or it is re-caught. The
# .8–.10 through-line is gate honesty: instances FOUR and FIVE of
# "green-but-not-measuring" — a `.tcyr` that passes against the broken code (so
# the STRUCTURAL axis is load-bearing), and a fixture whose ORDER made its axis
# unreachable, twice (dir_walk guarantees no order; a decoy appended after the
# real key is never reached). Also: qemu-user reports a FALSE thread-VA leak where
# real pi reports exactly 0. LIVE STATE (refreshed v6.6.1, 2026-09-08): cycc x86_64
# **1,247,608 B** (.text 1,090,832) · seed **29,024 B** (seed→cybs→cycc
# byte-identical) · check.sh **240 passed / 0 failed** · **301** .tcyr (68 in
# `crossos/`) · **144** shell gates under `tests/gates/<bucket>/*.sh` in 8 buckets —
# DERIVE with `find tests/gates -name '*.sh' | wc -l`, never increment · **102**
# lib/*.cyr · **84** programs/*.cyr · api-surface **5152** public fns · heap map
# **102** regions / 0 overlaps (use `sh tests/gates/memory/heapmap.sh`; a raw grep
# over the map comment says 145 because it also matches FREED markers) ·
# self_compile **731-734 ms** · **0** open issues · cross-OS SELFHOST_OK + crossos
# LIBTEST_OK on ecb / ach / cass / pi, real hardware. ⚠ The `vr01_` filename prefix
# was retired at v6.5.11 — the cross-OS selector is the `crossos/` DIRECTORY now.
#
# Refreshed 2026-07-06 at v6.4.10 — the v6.4.x SIMD COMPUTE ARC (x86 portion
# COMPLETE, PAUSED before aarch64 NEON Phase 5): f32v4 128-bit SSE (.4) + f32
# matmul fmadd/dot (.5) + integer vectors i8/i16/i32/i64 (.6) + value-form typed
# int ops & iv_dp8 int8 dot for b1.58 GEMM (.7) + f32v8 256-bit AVX2, the FIRST
# VEX/AVX the toolchain ever emits (.8) + f32v8 FMA/dot via 3-byte VEX
# vfmadd231ps (.9). Highest SIMD builtin token 151; structured-descriptor
# sentinels -2121 (f32v4) / -2153 (f32v8) in the reserved band ≤-2048; x86 VEX
# emitters in src/backend/x86/float.cyr. v6.4.10 interim: P1 kernel-blocker fix
# (bare top-level var X[N] silently 8× under-sized after the first bare stmt —
# two-step bootstrap) + distlib per-module read cap 256KB→1MB. Added 2 gotchas:
# the VEX vvvv-is-1's-complement-of-src1 invisible-wrong-register trap (disasm-gate
# every op) + FMA-needs-a-DIFFERENT-CPUID-leaf/bit-than-AVX2 (leaf 1 ECX.12 vs
# leaf 7 EBX.5); and the top-level-array-sizing two-step bootstrap + a bug fix
# legitimately shows codegen-diff>0 with status-diff=0. cycc ~1,057,568 B,
# self_compile ~561 ms, check.sh 130 gates.
