# ─── Design Patterns (patterns.cyml) ─── 7 entries ─────────────────
# Reusable design + convention patterns. Earn their slot when an
# agent is making a structural decision (API surface, dep
# distribution, hook wiring, version-source design).

# ship_now_swap_backend_later                 — Decouple stability contract from impl; ship API via C shim, swap to native later
# dist_bundle_stdlib_dep_convention           — Single-file dist/<name>.cyr; cyrius distlib produces; consumers fetch via cyrius deps
# heap_cap_growth_compiler_grows_to_fit_language — When stdlib pushes a cap, raise the cap. Not the other way around. Reshuffle methodology.
# version_string_via_generated_source_not_hardcoded — Route --version through src/version_str.cyr; bump-script writes; never sed source literals
# stdlib_hook_surface_via_fn_pointer_not_callback_registry — One hook fn-pointer + one symbol-resolver beats N per-concern setters
# object_mode_pic_codegen_no_textrel          — object; emits PIC via LEA [rip+disp32] + R_X86_64_PC32. glibc 2.38+ dlopen-safe.
# research_first_optimizer_dce_cfg_lessons    — Pre-v5.0 research roundup: what maps onto cyrius's single-pass no-IR shape

# ─── Process Methodology (methodology.cyml) ─── 22 entries ─────────
# How to debug, how to scope, how to verify slot premises, how to
# triage cross-repo bug reports. Earn their slot when an agent is
# starting a slot, debugging a regression, or scoping a fix.

# premise_check_at_slot_entry                 — Read code + run 5-line probe BEFORE adopting a pin's stated scope
# perf_test_dont_assume_correctness_isnt_perf — Correctness tests are not performance tests. Add benchmarks before shipping an "optimization."
# verify_outputs_not_just_exit_codes          — sed/grep returning 0 doesn't mean it changed anything. Diff/re-read to confirm.
# verify_slot_premise_before_investing        — Reproduce the failure + inspect the artifact (otool/objdump/xxd) before adopting suspect list
# triage_dep_boundary_per_row_checksum        — "Corrupts at scale" cross-repo: standalone replay + per-row checksum at every dep boundary
# ci_drift_detection_silent_skip_is_false_green — Silent SKIP in CI gates is False-PASS. Every gate must report PASS/FAIL/SKIP explicitly — and since 6.6.11 in its EXIT CODE (77), because `echo SKIP; exit 0` scored PASS.
# ci_drift_detection_orphaned_path_is_certain_drift — Code paths with no CI gate WILL accumulate silent drift (cx backend, helpers, etc.)
# anticipated_gotcha_pre_flight_v55x          — Record gotchas BEFORE an arc starts; update DURING; archive AFTER as field-notes bundle
# stdlib_dep_care_not_application_care        — A repo whose dist/<name>.cyr vendors into lib/ IS stdlib; public-surface changes = major bump + ecosystem grep
# real_flow_gate_vs_selfhost_placebo          — Self-host is a placebo for dir-walk/process/deps; run the real consumer flow (init→lib sync→deps→build→run) on real hardware (v6.0.63)
# stdlib_public_fn_addition_trips_three_hygiene_gates — Adding public fns to a lib file trips lint + api-surface + cyrdoc gates even when cycc is byte-identical (v6.4.2)
# grading_a_subprocess_by_its_printed_summary_instead_of_its_exit_status_makes_every_appended_gate_advisory — release-gate.sh grepped check.sh's summary line, never $?; every gate appended AFTER the check binary was advisory. Enumerate the gate set from BOTH sides (check.sh + CI yml) (v6.5.0/.1)
# before_concluding_a_fix_does_not_work_check_what_else_writes_the_same_record — A correct fix was reverted as "theory disproved" because a SECOND hand-rolled marker emitter overwrote the same record. Presence in the binary is not effect (v6.5.3)
# a_gate_whose_fixture_cannot_express_the_bug_is_vacuous_and_it_passes_on_the_broken_build_too — sign-efi's 512-byte (8-aligned) fixture made the Authenticode pad EMPTY, so correct and broken hash the same range. Any rounding/padding step needs a fixture on BOTH sides (v6.5.4)
# a_tcyr_can_pass_against_the_broken_code_so_the_structural_axis_is_the_load_bearing_one — thread_join's .tcyr drives the raw futex ABI, so it stays green on the broken build (131/0). A 1-in-150k race is not provable by hammering; read the FUNCTION (v6.5.8)
# a_fixtures_order_can_make_an_axis_unreachable_and_dir_walk_guarantees_no_order_at_all — coverage's unique-symbol-in-the-last-file axis passed against the truncating build; distlib's decoy appended AFTER the real key was never reached. Also: `grep -c` prints 0 AND exits 1 (v6.5.8/.10)
# a_gate_bar_derived_from_a_host_quantity_measures_the_machine_and_gets_worse_as_the_host_improves — `wall < n * floor / 2` divides through to "the op must cost under half a clock read": a fact about the CPU, not the library. Passed by 400x on Linux (1,330 ns read), RED 6/6 on ecb once THIS release took the Darwin read to 5 ns against a 2.698 ns op — while the chunking it policed worked perfectly (97 windows, 194 reads for 100,000 iterations). ⚠ It also PASSED through a pipe and failed on `>/dev/null`, which is how the runner invokes it: a verdict that moves with where stdout goes is a measurement of the machine. Repair is a COUNT (`bench_windows`), pinned closed-form on the scripted clock — never a looser constant. Audit tell: a threshold with no ABSOLUTE term degenerates as the host improves (v6.6.5)
# a_check_must_never_write_the_thing_it_checks_save_modify_restore_is_only_as_safe_as_the_restore — syscall_xlat_generated backed a tracked source up to mktemp, regenerated it IN PLACE, and on a full /tmp restored an EMPTY backup over it (7450 -> 0 bytes) while reporting it STALE. Fix the write, not the backup. ⛔ An audit by broken-TMPDIR + `git status` MISSED a gate whose probe-then-rm cleaned up after itself: audit in NORMAL mode and compare CTIMES (`find -cnewer`), with the pre-fix offenders as positive controls. Full disk without a mount: `trap '' XFSZ; ulimit -f 4` (v6.6.6)
# an_absolute_nanosecond_tripwire_measures_the_box_it_was_set_on_and_drifts_blind_even_there — `per < 250` ns read GREEN on a syscall-per-release mutex on real ecb 10/10 (a `__ulock_wake` is ~100 ns there); alloc_via's `< 14` ns read 13 on the WHOLE fix reverted, on the box that set it, because faster code moves good and bad down together. Time a reference in the same run (min of interleaved rounds) and state the property against it: pair < floor + ref/2; for plumbing, rebuild both shapes in the probe and require 2*VIA < FIX + PL. Mutation-prove on every host (v6.6.6)
# a_gates_scratch_space_must_be_provably_its_own_checked_mktemp_no_fixed_names_and_observe_shared_namespaces_by_pid — a bare `D=$(mktemp -d)` that fails makes every path root-absolute (a "0/12 checked" PASS; a box-wide `pkill -f /bin/victim`); a fixed /tmp name — local or on a remote host — is shared by concurrent check.sh runs (ecb Mach-O T3 rc=126); a snapshot-delta over /tmp/cyrius-* counts another run's build — scope by the CLI's pid. Tool side: O_TRUNC-then-check-the-count is too late; temp + fsync + rename (v6.6.6)

# ─── Internal Gotchas (gotchas.cyml) ─── 125 entries ────────────────
# Non-obvious traps an agent will hit when working on cyrius's
# compiler internals. Earn their slot when an agent is debugging a
# cyrius regression that doesn't fit a clean pattern.
# ⚠ The list below is a SELECTION, not the roster — it names ~30 of the 123 (re-derived 6.6.12).
# gotchas.cyml's own header carries the running count + live-state stamp and is
# the authority; grep that file, don't infer coverage from what appears here.

# flags_reflect_rax_is_emitter_state_so_a_load_after_an_eaddr_must_clear_it — x86 skips `test rax, rax` before a condition when `_flags_reflect_rax` says the last emitter set the flags; EADDR sets it and EFIELD_LOAD_W deliberately leaves it, so the 6.6.12 subscript's `if (a[i])` branched on the ADDRESS until its load cleared the flag. Also at 6.6.12, INTO existing entries: cybs refuses a CALL with more than six arguments (a bare `syntax error` at seed-derive [3/5]; a 7-param DEFINITION is fine), a factor arm that parses its own call clears `_cfo` AFTER the call (5th occurrence), EFIELD_LOAD_W records IR_RAW_EMIT for widths 1/2/4 only so a signed load went unrecorded under CYRIUS_IR=3 (6th emitted-bytes instance), and a hand-kept `SYS_WRITE` byte count silently truncated the PE routed-number note (8th cap instance)
# file_attribution_is_a_line_lookup_so_the_lexer_line_counter_is_a_security_boundary — `private` is decided by FM_FILEID(token line); a lexer that did not count a newline inside a string literal moved tokens into the neighbouring file and let a cross-file private call compile (CVE-55, 6.6.11) — third input to that lookup to be a bypass, after the span arithmetic (v6.5.3) and forged markers (CVE-45)
# two_passes_computing_the_same_fact_disagree_make_pass_one_the_authority — cyrius stamped fn visibility in pass 1 AND recomputed it in pass 2, and both halves were wrong: pass 1 skipped four definition kinds (impl methods, `mod` fns, anything after the first top-level statement, anything above the `private` line) so the check fell OPEN, while pass 2's `var` skip re-armed `public` and was masked only because the pass-1 bit was never CLEARED. ⭐ A stamping gap does not present as "too permissive" — it presents as a scatter: wrong ABI (a >8B struct param value-passed → SIGSEGV), wrong arity, wrong symbol NAME in a diagnostic, and FALSE refusals in ordinary include order, because everything downstream reads the same empty record. Fix: mark the file once before either pass, register per DEFINITION not per name, let pass 2 find its own entry by its `fn` token, clear the bit for a public definition, and keep a fail-CLOSED deferral under it (v6.6.5)
# a_cannot_pack_reason_deserves_the_same_scrutiny_as_the_bug — a filing deferred this fix on "a design decision on the name pool, with seed-derive exposure, across a 7-fork obligation". The decision was an 18-line function (mint without committing, reuse the existing string), the fork obligation two one-line calls each, and seed-derive was GREEN. Test: can you state the design decision as a question with a small number of answers? Then it is not a design decision, it is a thing you have not tried (v6.6.5)
# routing_a_new_caller_through_a_shared_helper_inherits_its_latent_bug — fixing a call path with no ABI handling by "route it through the shared helper the others use" traded a loud SIGSEGV for a SILENT wrong value: the helper took `&slot` unconditionally, which is wrong for a POINTER-mode struct local, and had been wrong on the ordinary `f(x)` path since v6.3.36 (printed 140545185808389 for 42). A shared helper's blast radius is measured over what people DO call it with — the set that avoids its bugs. Probe the new caller's shape against the helper FIRST, and read the VALUE, not the exit code (v6.6.5)
# one_call_syntax_is_not_one_call_path_enumerate_the_masks — cyrius marshals arguments on SEVEN argument loops (PARSE_FNCALL, the `s.m(a)` method path, the `return f(a)` tail path, and FOUR Win64 hidden-retptr vector receives) and each reads the callee's parameter masks independently. ⚠ This line said FOUR after the round that found the third; `grep -n '_try_push_struct_addr_arg(' src/frontend/` is the enumeration. The tell is TWO SPELLINGS DISAGREEING IN ONE PROGRAM, silently: `var r = f("abcde")` gave 5 while `return f("abcde")` gave 0 (no `str_from` wrap on the tail path), and `h.vmix(2, v, 3)` gave 927 against the free fn's 923 (a vector pushed as an int arg shifts every LATER argument by a register). The tail path alone has now been patched FIVE times for this (v6.3.36 struct params, v6.4.53 SIMD params, v6.5.1 overload dispatch, v6.5.2 cstring literals, v6.6.5 `: Str` literals). Enumerate the `_fnt_*mask` tables from their definition site; extract PARSE_FNCALL's arm into a shared helper rather than copying it. ⚠ And the CONTROL can be the broken one — the free fn this was compared against was itself written in tail position. ⛔ And a DIVERT is not automatically the safe direction: arming the `: Str` divert at any paren depth cost a SELF-RECURSIVE tail call its TCO, so `return deep(n-1, str_from("x"))` ran on 6.6.4 and SIGSEGV'd on the fix — read the divert's predicate off the helper you divert TO (v6.6.5). ⛔ v6.6.6: that grep finds only loops that ALREADY call a gate — PARSE_VAR's two `var p: S = f(..)` receives called none and were missed; enumerate by `ECALLPOPS(` instead. And walk (call syntax) x (return class) too: only the `var` receive supplied a >16 B struct's hidden retptr (v6.6.6) — and a destination that recognises a struct call by its TOKENS (`IDENT (`) cannot see a method call or an overloaded operator, whose callee is not named there: record the span at the emitter and match it at the destination (v6.6.6 review)
# process_entry_sp_parity_varies_with_argv_env_darwin_x86 — a process entry SP parity is a per-KERNEL fact, not an ABI fact: on Darwin x86_64 the initial rsp's 16-byte parity varies with the argv/env BYTE COUNT, so the same binary is aligned under one process name and misaligned under another (160/160 over a 20-argv0 x 16-env sweep on real ach). A landing must ESTABLISH the invariant (`and rsp,-16` after the r15 park, in BOTH x86 forks), never inherit it — third target in one release after PE and UEFI. Presents as a scatter of unrelated SHAPE failures with nothing naming the entry; and the cross-OS runner names every test `./_lt`, i.e. samples ONE parity, so a re-run is not a verification on Darwin (v6.6.5)
# nested_call_alignment_stack_machine — a stack-machine codegen is rsp-aligned only BETWEEN statements; a call nested in an argument or operand entered its callee 8 bytes off, the shift is INHERITED, and on PE the base itself was inverted so the STATEMENT-level calls were the wrong ones (v6.6.5)
# uefi_exit_must_restore_the_entry_rsp_not_adjust_it — UEFI exits through a bare `ret` and `ret` pops [rsp] ITSELF, so the exit must RESTORE the parked entry rsp; an `add rsp,8` give-back fixes only the depth it was computed for and left `syscall(60,x)` inside a fn body #GP'ing under OVMF. FOUR routes reach that ret (lib/alloc.cyr aborts through one). ⛔ TWO gate lessons: OVMF tolerates a misaligned CALL but not a misaligned RETURN and the smoke grepped for the PRINT; and its only fixture returns through its OWN asm `ret`, so it never tested the compiler's exit at all. ⛔ Plus the emission-order trap: fn BODIES ARE EMITTED BEFORE THE LANDING, so a flag set at the landing reads 0 in every fn body (v6.6.5)
# probe_row_reports_only_through_the_returned_argument — `snd(probe(), 0)` returns its SECOND argument and is the constant 0; four rows of 6.6.5's own alignment test were dead that way and passed against the broken compiler. Audit by rebuilding with the probe hardcoded to the FAILING value (v6.6.5)
# cyrius_top_level_statement_closes_the_declaration_window — struct/enum defs after the first top-level statement are `unexpected struct`; a struct-TYPED global there compiles but silently loses the annotation operator-overload dispatch keys on (v6.6.5)
# counter_model_gate_shares_the_defect — a gate that asks the compiler's own model to check that model reads GREEN: one mutant gives 0 desync reports and 24 CPU-measured misaligned calls (v6.6.5)
# a_generated_tables_two_halves_drawn_from_one_source_cannot_intersect — the raw-syscall diagnostic's better clause ("on ELF-aarch64 that number is `ptrace`") was DEAD CODE for 13 minors: the generator emitted a `_SYSX_MEANT` row only for numbers the aarch64 peer does NOT declare and built `_SYSX_ACTUALLY` from exactly those declared values, so the two lookups a consumer chains could never both hit. 43 warnings, 0 with the text. The tell is the PREDICATE, not the output — compile a probe with EVERY key and count how many reach the second lookup. Fix = a different source for the second half (the committed kernel table), and a generator reading an external fact HARD FAILS when it is missing rather than emitting an empty table that re-derives cleanly against itself (v6.6.5)
# an_arch_guarded_native_syscall_number_is_a_shadow_anywhere_not_just_in_the_peers — ESYSXLAT's shadow class had three gates watching it, all reading the same two stdlib peer files, while `lib/yukti.cyr` declared `SYS_STATFS = 43` under `#ifdef CYRIUS_ARCH_AARCH64` and the `43 -> 202` row made every call `accept()` on ARM. `raw_syscall_literals_routed.sh` EXEMPTS arch-guarded literals by construction, so every gate was doing its job and the union of their scopes had a hole shaped like a vendored fold. The discriminator must come from OUTSIDE the repo (does the row's DESTINATION mean that call on the kernel?), and a sweep whose real corpus is tiny needs a POSITIVE CONTROL, not a floor (v6.6.5)
# a_tracked_cross_compiled_binary_no_gate_rebuilds_goes_stale_then_wrong — `build/cycc-native-aarch64` is committed and shipped into every install slot and rebuilt by NOTHING; the pi gate leg builds fresh from source, so the tracked one has no freshness signal but its mtime. 60 releases stale, and a syscall renumber in the same release turned stale into WRONG (`sys_unlink` traced as `fanotify_mark`). Regenerate it in any release touching src/backend/aarch64 or the peers — deterministic and local, qemu is enough to self-host it to a fixpoint (v6.6.5)
# an_x86_hosted_cross_compiler_takes_the_hosts_arch_ifdef_arm — deleting an `#ifdef CYRIUS_ARCH_AARCH64` arm from cyrius's OWN source gave `IDENTICAL` for all SEVEN forks, `main_aarch64.cyr` included: those forks are x86-HOSTED cross compilers and the arch macros come from the compiler doing the compiling, so every aarch64 guard inside them is dead. Only `build/cycc-native-aarch64` moved, by exactly two bytes (the `movz` immediate). The trap is the reassurance — `IDENTICAL` across the fork sweep reads as "no-op, nothing to verify" and means the verification that matters has not run. Build the native compiler, or `qemu-aarch64 -strace` a cross-compiled probe (v6.6.5)
# a_gate_can_have_a_positive_control_and_still_read_green_over_an_empty_corpus — `aarch64_syscall_shadow.sh` axis 2 had a synthetic positive control for its SCANNER and floors on every INPUT (rows, peer declarations, kernel facts), and still printed `PASS … 0 declarations over 0 files` and exited 0 when its tree walk matched nothing — taking the one live cross-repo defect it names with it. A positive control proves the scanner; input floors prove the inputs; NEITHER says the corpus was visited. What closes it: re-derive a KNOWN live hit a DIFFERENT way (open that file by its own path), so a broken walk fails loudly and the check retires itself when the upstream fix lands (v6.6.5)
# assert_lte_zero_on_a_syscall_wrapper_accepts_every_failure — `assert_lte(sys_sched_yield(), 0, …)` is true for success (0) AND for every `-errno`, so the only assertion covering a newly-shipped wrapper could not fail: mis-declaring its syscall number scored 50/50, exit 0. The tell is the SHAPE — a bound a failure satisfies is not an assertion. Write the exact value per target (Linux/Darwin 0, PE -38) even though one loose bound "covers every target" (v6.6.5)
# a_check_that_reads_the_thing_it_guards_is_not_a_check_git_diff_index — `cyrius deps` proved a cached dep matched its tag with `git diff-index --quiet HEAD`, whose every input (stat cache, assume-unchanged/skip-worktree bits, core.* config, refs/replace) lives INSIDE the cache being judged. Wrong in both directions at once, and that is why one half hid the other: one `cp -a` refused 138 of 138 real checkouts (filed), while seven shapes of real tampering vendored at exit 0 (nobody files an accept). Fix = build the evidence yourself: `read-tree HEAD` into a PRIVATE throwaway index, then diff-files + `ls-files -o` + a gitlink scan (v6.6.5, CVE-43)
# overriding_an_untrusted_config_with_dash_c_is_not_enough_the_keys_that_matter_cannot_be_overridden — the same fix's first cut pinned five `-c` values on the cache's config and called the config handled; review then vendored tampered bytes at exit 0 EIGHT more ways, all inside `.git`: `core.worktree` (a pristine copy parked beside the tamper), a `filter.*.clean` driver — whose NAME is attacker-chosen, so there is nothing fixed to override, and which git RUNS — the same filter behind `include.path` (which `config --local --list` does not print), `.git/info/attributes` alone, `core.autocrlf` (cannot be forced off: a global autocrlf user has a legitimately CRLF tree), `extensions.worktreeConfig` + `.git/config.worktree` (a second config file the local listing also hides), and a clone of a DIFFERENT repo at the same name+tag. ⭐ Partition the knobs: what `-c` CAN override, override; what it cannot, REFUSE by name — and refuse it BEFORE the command that would run it (v6.6.5)
# a_hardening_check_that_reads_policy_complaints_as_integrity_failures_bricks_valid_inputs — `git fsck` exits 1 for `missingEmail` / `badDate` / `zeroPaddedDate` / `missingAuthor`, none of which says anything about whether an object hashes to its name; treating any non-zero as "object-store damage" would have made a dep with one old commit unresolvable FOREVER, and the advertised `rm -rf <cache>` re-clones the same objects. Same shape one line up: forcing `core.fileMode=true` OVERRODE git's own filesystem probe, so on vfat/exfat/9p (where the bit cannot be stored) every 755 entry read as tampered and `reset --hard` could not repair it. ⭐ When you harden a tool by forcing its settings, ask what the tool was telling you with the value you just overrode — and separate its POLICY opinions from its INTEGRITY ones (v6.6.5)
# one_identifier_two_legal_spellings_is_not_a_string_compare — the same fix compared `remote.origin.url` against the manifest with `==`, and `…/x` / `…/x.git` / `…/x/` are ONE repository on every forge: 19 live declarations across 11 repos refused, an untouched cache called tampered, which is the defect the release existed to FIX one layer up. Worse, no fixed point — following the printed `rm -rf` makes the OTHER consumer refuse, for ever. ⭐ An identity check between two strings written by different people needs the identity relation, not equality; normalise what the domain says is insignificant, then prove a genuinely different value still refuses. The CHANGELOG claim shared the blind spot too — it had been checked against the caches, not against the declaring manifests. And the same compare sat one fn over, on the COMMIT PIN lookup, where it does not refuse but silently TOFU-RE-PINS — grep the SHAPE, not the site (v6.6.5, CVE-43)
# an_argument_parser_per_verb_is_a_defect_per_verb — a filing about ONE flag on ONE verb (`cyrius lint --strict-deferrals`) was ~60 spellings across every verb and every delegated tool, because ~35 branches in cbt/cyrius.cyr each hand-rolled their own loop. Four faces: an undeclared `-` token becomes the OPERAND (`build s --strict` wrote the binary to a file NAMED `--strict`), a flag after the operand is DROPPED (`fmt f --chekc` REWROTE the file, exit 0), extra operands are dropped (`lint a b` linted one — ranga CI linted 1 of 41), and a literal `argv(2)` shifts under a global -q (`-q clean --dry-run` DELETED build/). ⭐ Severity lives in what the verb does when it proceeds anyway — sort the rows by SILENT-vs-LOUD and MUTATING-vs-not. Also: `--dry-run` was set AFTER `_auto_deps`, so deps.cyr's dry-run branch had never once been reachable; `run_tool` capped at 3 args, which is why cmd_lint was WRITTEN to forward only --strict + the file; and run_tool's fork/waitpid are -1 STUBS on PE, so lint/fmt/doc/vet/deny never spawned their tool on Windows at all (v6.6.5)
# gate_a_cli_with_a_hash_the_shell_computes — side effects measured by `{ find . ; find . -type f | xargs sha256sum ; } | sha256sum`, never by asking the tool. ⚠ A `find -type f` alone misses symlinks and a bare `mkdir`, and that blind spot hid a real `lib sync --dry-run` mkdir during development. Put the defect in the LAST operand (a mutant that iterates only operand 0 passes otherwise — that IS mutation M3); give the filed row a SECOND oracle from a different binary; derive the verb census from the source so a verb added later cannot escape; and record mutations as MEASURED — one row is honest that restoring flags.cyr's cap leaves this gate green and reds flags.tcyr instead, because the CLI does not use the stdlib parser (v6.6.5)
# could_not_measure_is_not_measured_false — three fail-opens and a hard-fail in one release, one shape: a probe that could not ASK treated the failure to ask as an answer. An unwritable directory read as "this filesystem cannot store the exec bit" (memoised per PROCESS, so one read-only dir disabled mode comparison for every dep — a chmod -x tamper accepted at rc 0), and on Windows `sys_fork` is `return -1`, so every git command fails and the new fail-CLOSED refusal hard-failed a pre-populated cache with a reason that is false. ⭐ Every probe has THREE outcomes: yes, no, I-could-not-ask. Name the third and fall back to another measurement of the same thing (git's own clone-time value), never to a guess (v6.6.5, CVE-43)
# a_conversion_layer_in_the_comparison_is_a_laundering_channel — `git diff-files` compares clean(working tree) with the blob, and `clean` is whatever the ATTRIBUTES say, so a `.gitattributes` CARRIED BY THE TAG (`* text=auto`) laundered a CRLF-only edit of a cached module: exit 0, changed bytes vendored. Refusing the cache-written `.git/info/attributes` did not cover it, because the tracked file is legitimate. ⭐ Compare RAW bytes as well (`hash-object --no-filters`), then require any difference to be EXPLAINED by re-materialising the path through the same conversion (`cat-file --filters`) — that keeps a legitimately CRLF checkout resolving instead of trading one false refusal for another (v6.6.5, CVE-43)
# two_axes_that_exist_because_the_ledger_could_not_prove_their_check — a mutant that reds NO axis means the code is dead or the fixture is right for the wrong reason, and both get written down as "verified" if the ledger is skipped; the deps-cache gate needed four such axes, and one mutant (drop `GIT_WORK_TREE`) still reds nothing and is KEPT as the layer that does not depend on having enumerated the right config key (v6.6.5)
# a_line_scanner_forgets_what_the_language_carries_across_lines — 6.6.5: cyrlint ran every rule on ONE line; a wrapped deferral, a wrapped initializer (a real silent zero, proved at runtime), a raw-newline string and wrapped call args all crossed it. Join the TEXT but keep the pointer EVIDENCE line-granular (block scope hid 1 of 3 filed cases, un-flagged 98/179); cache per-line verdicts (27 s → 0.26 s). Round 2: enumerate the shapes the PARSER accepts (`=` on the next line, `pub var`, `sys_open (`), a `#` is not always a comment (`#naked fn f() {` — cyrfmt flattened it too), and a check expecting "nothing" must prove the tool ran (a segfaulting cyrlint read PASS 77/77). Round 3: the unit is the STATEMENT (a header wraps anywhere; decls after `}` / after a wrapped `;`) and order is by OFFSET; a walk frontier keeps it linear; an output buffer sized for the input segfaulted cyrfmt; a fixed 64 KB read made sigil's doc gate judge 6 % of its bundle; the preprocessor executed directives inside multi-line strings too (filed; fixed 6.6.6 as PP_LEXST — and the newline reset that had to go was a blast-radius bound, so char literals had to become a state first)
# cx_bytecode_backend_is_cli_exposed_check_backend_dirs_before_declaring_a_feature_absent — The cyrius-x (cx) bytecode backend IS CLI-exposed: `--target=cx` (cbt/cyrius.cyr:437) and cxvm ships in cyrius.cyml `bins`, since v6.4.17–.22. The old "no CLI verb / cxvm uninstalled" framing is RETIRED — don't conclude a feature is absent from a grep miss, check src/backend/
# vex_encoding_vvvv_ones_complement_and_fma_cpuid_leaf — FIRST VEX/AVX the toolchain emits (f32v8 256-bit, v6.4.8/.9): the VEX vvvv field is the 1's-COMPLEMENT of src1 → wrong polarity assembles VALID but reads the WRONG register (invisible to self-host) → disasm-gate every new VEX op; FMA = CPUID leaf 1 ECX.12, a DIFFERENT leaf+bit than AVX2's leaf 7 EBX.5; in-tree decode.cyr NOT extended for VEX (pre-existing no-ModRM 0F mis-decode, P3)
# two_step_bootstrap_for_toplevel_array_sizing_and_legit_codegen_diff — v6.4.10: a change to how cycc sizes its OWN top-level `var X[N]` arrays (P1 kernel-blocker, was 8× under-sized after the first bare stmt) is a TWO-STEP bootstrap, same class as the W^X flip; and a real bug fix SHOULD show differential codegen-diff>0 WITH status-diff=0 — codegen-diff=0 on a behavior fix means it didn't fire

# slice_fn_local_layout_flip                  — Pre-§8 16-byte fn-locals overflowed past frame; v5.8.16 layout-flip fixes
# slice_high_half_regalloc_pin                — Phantom slot (no name) gets allocated to register; address-based memory I/O bypass
# tail_call_escape_addr_local                 — return helper(&local); — TCO epilogue deallocates frame; v5.8.16 skips TCO when & in args
# pointer_vs_inline_struct_dispatch           — PARSE_FIELD_LOAD auto-detects pointer-vs-inline via slot lli-1 sentinel; v5.8.17
# stale_fixed_cap_drift                       — Cap check drifts out of sync with allocation; recurring trap class
# stdlib_alloc_grow_step_must_cover_request   — Bump allocator's grow step must cover the requested size
# libssl_needs_fdlopen_not_dynlib_open        — pthread-using libs need glibc's TLS/TCB; use fdlopen, not dynlib
# sysv_odd_stack_args_rsp_alignment           — SysV requires rsp 16-aligned at CALL; odd nextra needs pre-pad
# pp_pass_helpers_take_src_base               — Preprocessor pass helpers must take src_base, not assume S+0 region
# ts_lex_jsx_lookahead_terminators            — TS arrow-fn lookahead must terminate at JSX construct close
# fn_keyword_in_param_position                — `fn` is reserved; using it as a param name surfaces error at the NEXT fn def
# lsp_globals_before_fn_definitions           — Top-level vars must be declared before fn bodies that reference them
# locname_staleness_duplicate_dispatch_paths  — Same locname-stash bug surfaces in EACH dispatch path; audit all when fixing one (v5.10.35 + v5.10.39)
# install_sh_cp_L_same_file_silent_fail       — install.sh cp -L collides with `cyrius deps` symlinks; set -e exits before symlink-update block (v5.10.37)
# stack_local_scratch_buffer_overflow_at_dispatch — Stack-scratch for compile-time name construction must size to LARGEST input, not typical (v5.10.39)
# heap_relocation_inside_input_buf_v51119     — Relocating tables into 0x0-0x100000 collides with input_buf; first compile silently works, second hangs (v5.11.19 Phase 1 misstep, caught by fixpoint check)
# cyrius_deps_global_symlink_wedge_v51117     — Pre-v5.11.17 `cyrius deps` resolved stdlib_dir from mutable ~/.cyrius/lib symlink; closed in deps.cyr::_dep_find_stdlib_dir rewrite
# macho_syscall_number_dual_definition_61_vs_217 — SYS_GETDENTS64 is 217 (x86/macos) AND 61 (aarch64); wrapper binds 61 by include order; macho ESYSXLAT missed 61→344 → arm64-macOS dir-walk EBADF. "Works in probe, fails in wrapper" = dup global, not codegen (v6.0.63)
# macho_output_basename_breaks_reproducible_cmp — Mach-O embeds the output basename, so same-source-to-different-names differs by name bytes (false non-reproducible); rebuild SAME name + hash UNSIGNED, never codesign-cmp (v6.0.63)
# ts_children_list_reserve_then_fill_corrupts — TS parser: never RESERVE a children list then parse elements into it (RESERVE doesn't advance the cursor → nested sub-lists stomp it). Use TS_CST_PUSH/TS_CST_FLUSH (collect-then-flush). Corrupt for years because --parse-ts never reads lists back (v6.1.10)
# ts_trailing_comma_generic_params_tsx — TS_PARSE_TYPE_PARAMS must accept a trailing comma before `>`: the `.tsx` disambiguation form `<T,>(x)=>x` failed to parse, blocking every generic arrow in a .tsx file (v6.1.10)

# ── v6.5.7–.10 (added by the 2026-08-07 sweep) ──
# esysxlat_is_a_linear_cmp_chain_so_an_entry_must_sit_below_every_entry_that_compares_the_number_it_produces — ESYSXLAT rewrites x8 in place and falls through, so an entry whose OUTPUT is a later entry's COMPARE is re-caught. The >=1000 cyrius-private alias band (1054 fchownat / 1049 chdir; 1000+native, self-documenting) exists because native 54 is the setsockopt shim and x86 260 is SYS_WAIT4 — both owned. One alias = FOUR edits (enum, a64 chain, macho chain, _macho_arm_routes) (v6.5.7)
# darwin_at_star_flags_diverge_from_linux_and_a_pure_renumber_xlat_passes_them_straight_through — AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW 0x20 / AT_SYMLINK_FOLLOW 0x40 / AT_REMOVEDIR 0x80 vs Linux 0x100/0x400/0x200. Pure-renumber entries pass flags through untouched, so a Linux value is EINVAL forever, silently: xrmdir never worked on macOS-arm64 since v6.5.2 (v6.5.7)
# the_macos_x86_stat_enum_was_a_mix_of_two_structs_because_only_the_field_that_prompted_the_fix_was_corrected — Backend maps stat(4)→Darwin 188 (legacy struct) but the enum carried stat64 offsets; only STAT_SIZE was ever corrected (v6.0.41). STAT_MODE read the low half of st_ino. One wrong offset means the WHOLE enum describes the wrong struct (v6.5.7)
# the_incdir_marker_rides_in_band_because_both_out_of_band_channels_are_dead_on_some_target — `#@incdir` on line 1: chdir breaks the root-relative dep prepend and `_read_env` is stubbed on Windows and cx. In-band ⇒ a hostile .cyr can write one ⇒ must be relative, `..`-free, and read ONLY at byte 0 (v6.5.7)
# qemu_user_reports_a_false_thread_va_leak_because_proc_self_statm_measures_the_host_process — ~1,665 residual pages/thread under qemu vs exactly 0 on real pi. Also: VA not RSS; poll until settled (a spin loop is not a synchronisation primitive); assert ZERO, not "less" (v6.5.8)
# negating_at_i64_min_is_a_no_op_so_every_while_n_gt_0_decimal_formatter_printed_a_bare_minus — `n = 0 - n` is a no-op at i64::MIN, so `> 0` skips the whole digit loop: str_from_int(i64::MIN) was "-" and bayan emitted `{"n":-}`. 12 sites, two inside cycc (PRNUM, _emit_decimal). fmt_hex had been fixed for this at v6.4.69 and the decimal siblings were never brought along (v6.5.8)
# an_allocator_returning_0_is_not_an_error_channel_when_the_type_system_has_no_option — arena exhaustion was a SIGSEGV three layers away; the policy field (NULL/GROW/SPILL/ABORT) is one field, not three features. GROW retains chunks across reset; arena_free left the policy set so a "freed" growable arena still grew (v6.5.9)
# cyrius_does_not_inline_so_a_one_load_accessor_on_a_dispatch_path_is_a_real_call_frame — alloc_via 15.1 ns of which 5.1 was two accessor CALLS each performing one load64. 15–16 → 11 ns. ⚠ `_bump_alloc`/`_bump_reset` look like the same trampoline and are NOT — they ADAPT ARITY; removing them corrupts the call (v6.5.10)
# the_distlib_deps_sidecar_scanned_includes_not_the_declaration_and_a_wrong_sidecar_switches_off_cyriuss_own_consumer_check — setu emitted 8 leaves against a declared 12, and an under-declaring consumer then built OK where a correct sidecar hard-errors. Union declaration+scan for the BASE bundle only; profiles keep the pruned inference or they over-report (v6.5.10)

# ─── Retros (retros/) ─── narrative ────────────────────────────────
# Per-version chronological narrative — feature lists, release-arc
# retrospectives, post-arc reflections. Duplicates CHANGELOG.md /
# completed-phases.md content; preserved here as cyml for vidya
# consumers. Read for backstory; for current work use the topical
# files above.

# ⚠ retros/ STOPS AT v6.1.x. There is no v6.2.x / v6.3.x / v6.4.x / v6.5.x retro —
# for those cycles the narrative source is CHANGELOG.md (canonical) plus
# docs/development/completed-phases.md and roadmap_6.md. Don't read the retro list
# below as coverage of the v6 line; it covers roughly its first fifth.
#
# retros/pre_v3.cyml          — v0.9–v1.x feature lists (5 entries)
# retros/v3.cyml              — v3.0 retrospective + v3.3.x–v3.4.x release arcs (9 entries)
# retros/v4.cyml              — v4.0.0 reflections + v4.8.x cleanup-ramp handoff (3 entries)
# retros/v5_chronicle.cyml    — Per-cycle v5.x feature lists (1 entry — v56x_features at this writing)
# retros/v58x_agent_perspective.cyml — Agent's view from the v5.8.x slices true-completion sub-arc
# retros/v58x_back_half.cyml  — v5.8.x back half (slots .49–.65) — Unicode 17 fold, heap two-step bootstraps, foldin closeout
# retros/foldin_arc_v57_v59.cyml — Cross-cycle pattern: sandhi (v5.7.0) / vani (v5.8.0) / niyama (v5.9.0) — receipts + framework, marked for language-agent extension on niyama-direct experience
# retros/v59x.cyml             — v5.9.x cycle close (44 patches / 2 days; sovereignty pass + agnosys 1.1.12 cascade + Mach-O ARM64 fnptr ASLR fix + cx Phase 2c + lib/regression carve-out; lazy-defer feedback sharpened to revised acceptance principle)
# retros/v510x.cyml            — v5.10.x cycle close (50 slots / 2026-05-06 → 2026-05-11; REAL TYPE SYSTEM 5-phase arc + typed-simd value-type ABI 11-phase arc + struct-byval 3-phase arc + compile-time-perf miniarc; cc5 753,768 → 804,472B / +50,704B; +12 cyrius test gates; PE premise debunk)
# retros/v511x.cyml            — v5.11.x cleanup minor through .20 (stdlib annotation arc / 9-sibling foldin / per-repo isolation Part 1 / kybernet 2-part bundle with honest audit-driven split / bote streaming arc 3→1 collapse / RFC 6455 §4.1 fix / slot map consolidation pattern; cc5 804,472 → 804,456B / -8B from string-literal deltas; +1 cyrius test gate (socket_syscalls.tcyr))
# retros/v60x.cyml             — v6.0.x cycle (CLOSED at v6.0.91, 91 patches): cybs/cycc rename ceremony (names forever) + native TLS 1.2/1.3 client+server (Cloudflare + OpenSSL interop) + CYRIUS_TARGET_AGNOS userspace target (boot-to-prompt) + the macOS/Windows hardening slate; defining thread = verification discipline evolving from hello-world placebo → real on-target self-host gate (.45) → real consumer-flow functional gate (.63, which surfaced + fixed the arm64-macOS dir-walk 61→344 bug)
# retros/v61x.cyml             — v6.1.x cycle "Backend Codegen Multi-Arc". ⚠ The file covers only through .11 and was written mid-cycle; the minor in fact CLOSED at 6.1.41, so .12–.41 are unnarrated here (CHANGELOG is the source): PIE position-independent codegen on x86_64 (.6) + aarch64 (.8) via --pie + the .gnu.hash dynlink migration (.9) + Phase D the TS/TSX→JS emitter cycc --emit-js (.11 on the AST allocator fix .10); defining lesson = a retained AST is only as correct as its first real reader (the TS parser shipped a corrupt nested-list AST for years because nothing walked it until the JS emitter)
